      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Interstate 80 and I‑287 intersect in the center of the CDP, a key crossroads for regional traffic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parsippany_(CDP)%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Route 202 runs through Parsippany CDP, leading north to Boonton and southwest to Morris Plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parsippany_(CDP)%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The entire CDP lies within the Passaic River watershed, draining north into the Rockaway River and southeast into Eastmans Brook.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parsippany_(CDP)%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1702, New Jersey unified under Queen Anne, a historical backdrop that shaped the region where Parsippany now sits.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
